Normal argument parser for the shared Warp executable across all channels.

Oz commands are subcommands of this parser, so invoking an `oz` symlink does not require a mode flag. Warp Control uses its separate [`local_control::ControlArgs`] parser, selected before this parser sees the arguments.

Usage: warpctrl [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  agent                               Interact with Oz
  environment                         Manage cloud environments [aliases: e]
  mcp                                 Manage MCP servers
  run                                 Manage runs
  model                               Manage available models
  memory-store                        Manage memory stores
  memory                              Manage memories
  login                               Log in to Warp
  logout                              Log out of Warp
  whoami                              Print information about the logged-in user
  integration                         Manage integrations [aliases: i]
  schedule                            Create and manage scheduled Oz agents. Scheduled agents run a user-defined task periodically, according to a cron schedule
  secret                              Manage secrets
  federate                            Issue and manage federated identity tokens
  artifact                            Manage artifacts
  api-key                             Manage API keys
  runner                              Manage cloud agent runners
  completions                         Generate shell completions for your shell to stdout.
  dump-debug-info, --dump-debug-info  Print debugging information and exit
  dump-settings-schema                Print the JSON schema for the current Warp channel's settings and exit
  help                                Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --api-key <API_KEY>
          API key for server authentication
          
          [env: WARP_API_KEY]

      --output-format <OUTPUT_FORMAT>
          Set the output format

          Possible values:
          - json:   Output as JSON
          - ndjson: Output as newline-delimited JSON
          - pretty: Output as human-readable text
          - text:   Output as plain text
          
          [env: WARP_OUTPUT_FORMAT=]
          [default: pretty]

      --debug
          Enable debug logging

      --crash-recovery-mechanism <CRASH_RECOVERY_MECHANISM>
          Crash recovery mechanism to use if we detect the parent process terminated
          
          [possible values: force-x11, force-dedicated-gpu, disable-opengl, force-vulkan]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Examples:

  $ warpctrl agent run --prompt "Build anything"

  $ warpctrl mcp list

Learn more:
* Use warpctrl help to learn more about each command
* Read the documentation at https://docs.warp.dev/reference/cli
